=== COVERAGE LIMIT OF A 3s WINDOW — read this ===
A 3s window holds roughly 100 frames. The scheduled intra
refresh is every 240 frames, so this certification
typically contains NO scheduled cut, and asserts A2 (intra only
on a scheduled index), A3 (cuts paired across views) and A4 (no
scheduled cut skipped) VACUOUSLY. What it does prove on real
bytes from this image: A1 no mid-stream IDR, A5 own-slot refs
and self-marking, A6 one contiguous frame_num chain, A7 chain
depth within bound, and that every picture decodes without a
black frame.
The cut schedule itself is covered by CI against golden vectors
(tests/xrdp/test_avc444_ltr.c: test_ltr_dpb_scheduled_paired_cut
_both_modes, test_ltr_schedule_observed_vs_requested,
test_ltr_cut_sequence_byte_exact). Do NOT lengthen this window
to chase A2-A4 -- that is the 10x tax this file exists to
remove, and CI already pins the logic byte-exactly.
